Here is a SystemVerilog module for an LDPC (Low-Density Parity-Check) encoder for FPGA implementation:

```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in,
    output wire data_out
);

reg [7:0] state;
reg [7:0] next_state;
reg [7:0] output_data;

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
    begin
        state <= 0;
        next_state <= 0;
        output_data <= 0;
    end else
    begin
        next_state <= state;
        output_data <= data_in ^ state;
        state <= next_state;
    end
end

assign data_out = output_data;

endmodule
```

This module implements a simple LDPC encoder with a 8-bit input and output data. The state machine is used to control the encoding process, and the output data is the encoded version of the input data.

